Orbit Go + MyGo experimental macOS test
CI version __VERSION__ / source __SOURCE_COMMIT__ / __ARCHLABEL__ (__ARCH__) / 2026-10-25

THIS IS NOT A RELEASE, NOT FEATURE-COMPLETE, AND NOT NATIVE-MAC-ACCEPTED.
It is a download for later manual testing, assembled in GitHub Actions Linux.
No user's Mac was accessed. No signing key or security workaround is included.

Read KNOWN-LIMITS.txt first for concrete implementation gaps in this fixed build.

QUICK START
1. Use Apple Silicon (arm64) for M-series Macs, Intel (amd64) for Intel Macs.
   These exact binaries declare macOS 13.0 minimum; actual OS compatibility
   has not been established. Do not select an older OS or rely on Rosetta.
2. Extract the ZIP. Keep its folder and .app contents together.
3. Optional: run Verify.command. It checks all bundled file hashes and inspects
   the architecture. It does not launch Orbit or change macOS security.
4. Open Launch.command. This starts the .app through the isolated launcher,
   prints the temporary test-data and log locations, then opens the native UI.
   Alternatively open Orbit Go Test.app; it uses the same isolated defaults,
   but Finder will not show the printed log path. Use Launch.command first.
5. No Pi runtime is selected by default. A missing-Pi/connection error is
   expected, not hidden by a fake server. You can inspect the native shell,
   settings, the synthetic Files workspace and integrated terminal without
   connecting an AI provider. Successful LLM inference is NOT established.

This app is not Developer ID signed or notarized. macOS may refuse to run it.
Stop and report the exact security/error message if blocked. Do not remove
quarantine, disable Gatekeeper, change OS security, or re-sign this package
as a workaround. Signing/notarization and native acceptance remain open work.
The Go/ upstream arm64 bytes contain code-signature commands, but that is NOT
Developer ID identity verification, notarization, or validation by this task.

ISOLATION AND SIDE EFFECTS
Every launch creates a new mode-0700 /tmp/orbit-go-test.XXXXXXXX directory.
It gets a synthetic HOME, .pi/agent, cache/config/temp directories and a small
workspace copied from the bundle. Existing credentials, session histories,
SSH_AUTH_SOCK and environment API keys are not inherited. The launcher does
not install Pi, Node, Git or gh; does not import auth; and does not auto-delete
its test data. Temporary test data may be removed by macOS/reboot. Do not use
this location for important work. To clean up, quit Orbit and move only the
printed test-data folder and extracted package to Trash yourself.

THIS IS NOT A SECURITY SANDBOX. The app, tools and terminal still run with your
normal user permissions. macOS may create ordinary LaunchServices/app metadata
or request permissions. Bundled test data is disposable; do not open important
projects or supply credentials for the first smoke test. The integrated zsh
can read system-wide shell startup files. Native open/reveal/browser actions
can affect other apps. '--offline' suppresses catalog/startup-update checks,
not every network request and not model inference after explicit setup.
The app's release updater is unconfigured for these development binaries.
This test .app has the distinct identifier dev.orbit.go.experimental.__APP_SUFFIX__,
not the original Rust Orbit identifier. Native app/notification identity
behavior may therefore differ from the production reference.

OPTIONAL REAL PI RPC TEST (SEPARATE RUNTIME)
Pi 1.4.0 is the protocol-test pin; Pi is not included in this ZIP. If you already
have an appropriate Pi runtime, use an absolute path. In Terminal, change to
this extracted directory, then run:
  ./Launch.command --pi "/absolute/path/to/pi"
If Pi is a Node-script installation, Pi 1.4.0 requires Node >=22.19.0, which
must be available to that installation (standard Homebrew/system paths are
provided). No dependency is
automatically installed. Prefer the official standalone Pi distribution where
available. See https://github.com/earendil-works/pi for official instructions.
No existing ~/.pi data is copied: logging in is a separate, explicit action.
For an expendable copy of a project only:
  ./Launch.command --pi "/absolute/path/to/pi" --workspace "/absolute/path/to/disposable-copy"
That project is real, and editor autosave, Git, terminal or agent actions may
change it. Configuration isolation does not protect workspace files.
Do not point this initial test at your original working project.

WHAT WAS VERIFIED HERE
- Binaries were built from the recorded Git commit by GitHub Actions, with
  Go 1.27.3, CGO_ENABLED=0 and the canonical compatibility wrapper.
- Default runtime inputs are fingerprint-checked against frozen a7aa6cf.
  Packaging/version metadata differs; actual new executable hashes are recorded.
- Both dylibs match the SHA-256 pins in mygo-plugin.json from MyGo 9c69cf8.
- Thin Mach-O architecture, macOS deployment metadata, dynamic link paths and
  all 92 Ghostty functions required by the Go binding were checked statically.
- The dylib links only macOS libSystem. MyGo core/editor are Go code plus
  macOS system frameworks; no separate core/editor dylib is missing.
- Icons, fonts, locales and Orbit Pi extensions are embedded in orbit-bin.
- Linux aggregate tests and six cross-builds are recorded in provenance.
  Pi 1.4.0 is a top-level npm test dependency pin, not a repository-locked
  transitive graph; its resolved package-lock hash is recorded. Pi is not bundled.

WHAT WAS NOT VERIFIED
- macOS launch, dyld load, runtime ABI layout check, Metal/CoreText drawing,
  notifications, IME, clipboard, file panels, PTY, native keyboard/focus,
  actual Pi inference or feature/pixel parity on either Mac architecture.
- Native Mac CI/startup acceptance. GitHub Actions Linux aggregate tests and
  cross-builds are recorded separately; those do not establish Mac execution.
- Developer ID signing/notarization, app distribution acceptance, update feed.
Compilation, static validation and Linux testing are not native Mac acceptance.

SUGGESTED MANUAL SMOKE TEST
- Launch the matching architecture; record macOS version, architecture and error.
- Confirm window/chrome, resize, Cmd+, settings, Cmd+P palette, close/reopen, quit.
- Open the sample README.md and hello.go. Type/undo/redo and confirm autosave
  only changes the temporary sample workspace. Try IME and selection separately.
- Open terminal with Cmd+J. Check that 'pwd' and 'printf "%s\n" "$HOME"' point
  to the temporary test tree before running only harmless test commands.
- Check text rendering and screenshot mismatches without claiming parity.
- If you explicitly selected Pi, check get_state/start, streaming, cancellation,
  session reload and errors using a disposable project. No live inference has
  been pre-validated, and provider use can cost money.

For feedback, share the architecture, macOS version, launch error and relevant
log excerpt. Inspect logs/screenshots and redact personal data before sharing.
No telemetry or automatic log upload is added by this package.

PACKAGE CONTENTS
Orbit Go Test.app: launcher + exact Go binary + pinned Ghostty dylib + test data.
Launch.command: isolated launcher entry point.
Verify.command: read-only package integrity check (hashes are not signatures).
provenance/: source/binary linkage, actual build-info and static audit.
licenses/: Go/runtime, MyGo/Ghostty, third-party and embedded-resource notices,
including the unresolved historical Waku-attribution caveat. No legal clearance
for the historical Rust reference is asserted.
SHA256SUMS: all distributed files except itself. Outer ZIP hash is supplied
separately with delivery metadata.
